[task.2.2]
title      = "Run the gateway in kernel mode on the existing endpoint app, served only at the router URL"
status     = "pending"
wave       = 2
requires   = ["2.1", "2.4", "2.8"]
blocked_on = "the CNAME record api.mainnet-beta.router.paxeer.network in the paxeer.network zone pointing at the fly.dev name of the app that human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml declares, added by the owner"
do_1       = "Switch the Redis certificate and the gateway's outbound root in one deploy window, because the gateway takes one outbound DER root and cannot verify Redis between two deploys: when the served chain of the Redis app of human/wallet/deploy/redis.toml does not end at the internal CA root, issue its certificate through the gateway-redis row of tools/bringup/ca.sh with the Redis app's .internal name by the several-machine path of ca_issue, because the Redis image reads its key from a [[files]] secret, and stage REDIS_TLS_CERT, REDIS_TLS_KEY and REDIS_TLS_CA with flyctl secrets import --stage; then import ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA as the internal CA root on the endpoint app, deploy the Redis app on its new certificate and at once deploy the endpoint app of do_2, so the gateway's one outbound root serves both Redis and the kernel backends."
do_2       = "Make human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml run the gateway in kernel mode on its plain listener: core_agent_boundary and independent_receipt_authority at the kernel app's .internal name over mTLS with the client identity issued through the gateway-client row of tools/bringup/ca.sh and imported as Fly secrets, ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA the internal CA root, LAYERX_GATEWAY_PAXEER_RPC_URLS naming at least two serving RPC names that the rpc-nodes subcommand shows at the head, the existing Redis app, and at least two machines in two regions, with LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_URL left unset so that backend reports not_configured until task 2.6 sets it; add every new [env] name to human/wallet/deploy/env with one line each and deploy it."
do_3       = "Add the router URL to the app with flyctl certs add and print the CNAME target for the owner; the app's fly.dev name is that target only and is written nowhere else."
do_4       = "Add the router subcommand: through the router URL eth_chainId 0x7d, px_getNetwork kernel.available true, lx_getAccount answering a read for a bound account and /readyz with every configured backend up, and the Redis round trip reported from a machine in each region; then the wallet gateway's /readyz reporting its rpc pool up with the router URL first in its RPC_URLS."
do_5       = "Only after the router checks of do_4 pass: set HYPERPAXEER_RPC_URL to https://api.mainnet-beta.router.paxeer.network and RPC_URLS to the router URL followed by the serving RPC names on the wallet gateway app of human/wallet/deploy/gateway.toml with flyctl secrets import on standard input from the operator host, which restarts its machines, update both lines of human/wallet/deploy/env to say so, and set the wallet PWA's NEXT_PUBLIC_PAXEER_RPC_URL on Railway to the router URL and redeploy the PWA."
