do_1       = "Once approved, add that location to the archive node's apiN vhost, check nginx -t and reload; write docker/platform-indexer/Dockerfile and docker/platform-indexer/Dockerfile.dockerignore building layerx-indexer from platform/hosted/indexer, and platform/hosted/indexer/fly.toml for a new Fly app: one machine with a volume holding the SQLite LAYERX_INDEXER_DB with daily snapshots and retention, LAYERX_INDEXER_LISTEN on [::] with its LAYERX_INDEXER_TLS_* listener material under the internal CA at the app's .internal name from a new indexer row of tools/bringup/ca.sh, no public service and no public IP, LAYERX_INDEXER_EVM_URL the archive node's public RPC name with LAYERX_INDEXER_EVM_CHAIN_ID 125, LAYERX_INDEXER_COMET_URL that location's https URL, both CA DERs ISRG Root X1 as [decision] public_roots pins it, LAYERX_INDEXER_RELAY_URL https://archive.paxeer.network, and LAYERX_INDEXER_START_BLOCK the archive node's first retained block read from the node at run time."
do_2       = "Before the live machine starts, read PAXSCAN_DATABASE_PUBLIC_URL from the explorer's Railway Postgres into a Fly secret of the indexer app on standard input without printing it, and run layerx-indexer backfill --cutover-height at the archive node's head read at run time in a one-off machine of the app on its volume, so the backfill from LAYERX_INDEXER_START_BLOCK up to the cutover is verified block by block against the archive node; then deploy the live machine on the same volume, which resumes at the cutover plus one."
do_3       = "Import LAYERX_GATEWAY_INDEXER_URL, the indexer's https .internal name, as a Fly secret of the endpoint app of human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml on standard input from the operator host, which restarts the router's machines."
do_4       = "Add the indexer subcommand: inside the indexer machine its listener answers over TLS under the internal CA, the app holds no public IP, its backfill cursor has reached the cutover, and through the router URL lx_getHistory, px_getHistory and px_getUnifiedHistory each answer a known account's history."
verify_cmd = "timeout 15m tools/bringup/check-live.sh indexer"
symbols    = ["check_indexer"]
touches    = ["docker/platform-indexer/Dockerfile", "docker/platform-indexer/Dockerfile.dockerignore", "platform/hosted/indexer/fly.toml", "tools/bringup/ca.sh", "tools/bringup/check-live.sh"]
tests      = ["tools/bringup/check-live.test.sh"]
reqs       = ["20.1", "20.2"]

[task.4.21]
title      = "Serve the hpx registry at node.hyperpaxeer.com from a Fly app and retire it from the hpx host"
status     = "pending"
wave       = 4
requires   = ["4.14", "0.5"]
blocked_on = "the CNAME record node.hyperpaxeer.com in the hyperpaxeer.com zone pointing at the fly.dev name of the app that hpx/hosting/fly.toml declares, in place of its current record, added by the owner"
do_1       = "Extend docker/hpx-registry/Dockerfile and its Dockerfile.dockerignore with nginx, the landing page, logo and fonts of hpx/hosting and hpx/hosting/nginx-fly.conf, which carries the locations and the /api/register rate limit of hpx/hosting/nginx.conf on a plain listener on [::]:8080 with real_ip_header Fly-Client-IP and X-Forwarded-For set to that address, and add docker/hpx-registry/entrypoint.sh as a root init that starts nginx and the registry on loopback under its user and exits when either exits."
do_2       = "Write hpx/hosting/fly.toml for a new Fly app: one machine with one volume at /srv/hpx holding the artifacts and the node directory, because the directory has one writer, the http_service on 8080 with /healthz as its check, and HPX_REGISTER_TOKEN streamed over ssh from HPX_HOST's /etc/hpx-registry.env into flyctl secrets import on standard input on the operator host; deploy it, stream the current release artifacts and the node directory from HPX_HOST into the volume through flyctl ssh console, verify checksums.txt, add node.hyperpaxeer.com with flyctl certs add and print the CNAME target for the owner."
do_3       = "Once the record resolves to the app and the hpx subcommand passes against it, remove the hpx vhost, the registry unit and /etc/hpx-registry.env from HPX_HOST, drop HPX_HOST from the host-map roles of tools/bringup/check-live.sh and from the fixtures of tools/bringup/check-live.test.sh and tools/bringup/sync-fleet.test.sh, and document in hpx/README.md that a release assembled by hpx/publish.sh is streamed into the app's volume through flyctl ssh console."
do_4       = "Extend the hpx subcommand: node.hyperpaxeer.com is an explicit CNAME to the fly.dev name of the app hpx/hosting/fly.toml declares, the landing page answers 200 beside the /healthz, checksums.txt and /api/nodes checks of task 4.14, and HPX_HOST no longer serves the name."
verify_cmd = "timeout 10m tools/bringup/check-live.sh hpx"
symbols    = ["check_hpx"]
touches    = ["docker/hpx-registry/Dockerfile", "docker/hpx-registry/Dockerfile.dockerignore", "docker/hpx-registry/entrypoint.sh", "hpx/hosting/nginx-fly.conf", "hpx/hosting/fly.toml", "hpx/README.md", "tools/bringup/check-live.sh", "tools/bringup/check-live.test.sh", "tools/bringup/sync-fleet.test.sh"]
tests      = ["tools/bringup/check-live.test.sh", "tools/bringup/sync-fleet.test.sh"]
reqs       = ["18.4"]

[task.4.22]
title      = "Move the public full node off the validator host onto its own server"
status     = "pending"
wave       = 4
requires   = ["0.5", "4.14"]
blocked_on = "the owner's server for the full node, added to RPC_HOSTS in the private host map as an ssh destination, and the owner's move of the DNS record of the apiN name that a validator host serves today to that server's address"
do_1       = "On the new server install hpx with hpx/get-hpx.sh, set up a full node with HPX_TYPE=fullnode hpx setup against node.hyperpaxeer.com and let it state-sync to the head, and install nginx with the apiN vhost the validator host serves today; once the owner's record resolves to the new server, run certbot for the name there, check nginx -t and reload."
do_2       = "Once the name answers eth_blockNumber within ten blocks of the head from the new server, stop and disable the full-node unit on the validator host, never a validator unit, remove its apiN nginx site and certificate there, and drop the validator host from RPC_HOSTS in the host map; when task 4.2 has already run, render and install the serving search sidecar of task 4.2 on the new server as for every serving RPC name."
do_3       = "Add the rpc-placement subcommand: each of the sixteen public RPC names resolves to an RPC_HOSTS destination that is not in VALIDATOR_HOSTS and answers eth_blockNumber within ten blocks of the highest answer, and over ssh no validator host runs a full-node unit or listens on a public HTTP or HTTPS port, never printing an address."
verify_cmd = "timeout 10m tools/bringup/check-live.sh rpc-placement"
symbols    = ["check_rpc_placement"]
touches    = ["tools/bringup/check-live.sh"]
tests      = ["tools/bringup/check-live.test.sh"]
reqs       = ["1.2", "18.3"]

[task.4.23]
title      = "Run the four x-websearch attestors as private Fly apps and remove them from the validator hosts"
status     = "pending"
wave       = 4
requires   = ["4.2", "0.6"]
blocked_on = "the owner's approval of moving the four registered attestor keys, with their submitter and receiver keys, from the validator hosts into the volumes of the four Fly attestor apps, and the owner's sealed offline copy of those keys before the validator-host copies are removed"
do_1       = "Add socat and docker/x-websearch/entrypoint.sh to docker/x-websearch/Dockerfile: the entrypoint runs as root, chowns the mounted /data volume, the config and the key files to uid 65532, drops privileges to 65532 with setpriv, starts one socat per peer from a loopback port to that peer app's .internal name on port 8480 and the x-websearch process, and exits when any of them exits, so Fly Machines restart the machine."
do_2       = "Write interop/deploy/x-websearch/attestor-1.toml to attestor-4.toml, one Fly app each with an app name distinct from the wallet attestor apps of human/wallet/deploy: one machine with a volume at /data holding the config and the keys, no service and no public IP; extend tools/bringup/xweb-config.sh with the Fly attestor kind rendering each config with listen [::]:8480, peers the loopback hop URLs of the other three, gateway.endpoint https://api.mainnet-beta.router.paxeer.network/rpc, the kernel's sequencer id and public key, the registered asset ids, evm a serving RPC name and the kernel block (endpoint the router's /rpc, the topics, submitter_did the attestor's receiver DID and the fee limit)."
do_3       = "With the owner's approval, migrate one slot at a time so at least three of the four signers stay live throughout: for slot N stop and disable x-websearch@N on its validator host, then create that slot's Fly app and volume, stream its registered attestor key with its submitter and receiver keys over ssh from the validator host into the volume through flyctl ssh console without printing them, deploy it and probe its /health over the private network, and move to slot N+1 only after that passes; once the four apps answer /health and the owner holds the sealed copy, remove the configs and keys from both validator hosts, and make the validators subcommand check that nothing listens on 8480 or 8481 on any validator host in place of the loopback /health check of task 0.6."
do_4       = "Add the xweb-attestors subcommand: each of the four apps runs one started machine with its volume and no public IP, answers /health inside its machine through flyctl ssh console and reaches each peer through its hop, and no validator host runs an x-websearch unit."
verify_cmd = "timeout 15m tools/bringup/check-live.sh xweb-attestors"
symbols    = ["xweb_config", "check_xweb_attestors"]
touches    = ["docker/x-websearch/Dockerfile", "docker/x-websearch/entrypoint.sh", "interop/deploy/x-websearch/attestor-1.toml", "interop/deploy/x-websearch/attestor-2.toml", "interop/deploy/x-websearch/attestor-3.toml", "interop/deploy/x-websearch/attestor-4.toml", "tools/bringup/xweb-config.sh", "tools/bringup/check-live.sh"]
tests      = ["tools/bringup/check-live.test.sh"]
reqs       = ["13.3", "1.2"]

[task.4.26]
title      = "Apply the owner's ruling on the account-derivation signing origin"
status     = "pending"
wave       = 4
requires   = ["0.3"]
blocked_on = "the owner's ruling whether the account-derivation message names paxportwallet.com in place of app.paxeer.network, which changes every derived account, or keeps app.paxeer.network and serves that name as a redirect to paxportwallet.com; and, for the redirect, the CNAME record app.paxeer.network in the paxeer.network zone pointing at the fly.dev name of the app that interop/deploy/search-front/fly.toml declares, added by the owner"
do_1       = "When the ruling names paxportwallet.com, change the message together in agent/crates/layerx-crypto/src/account_derivation.rs, agent/sdk/python/layerx_sdk/account_derivation.py, agent/sdk/typescript/src/account-derivation.ts, platform/sdk/conformance/fixtures/account-derivation-v1.json, the default of platform/hosted/human/material.py and its test platform/hosted/human/test_material.py, and the signing warning of docs/site/docs/concepts/one-account.md."
do_2       = "When the ruling keeps app.paxeer.network, add a server block for app.paxeer.network to interop/deploy/search-front/nginx.conf answering 308 to https://paxportwallet.com with the path kept, add the name to the search front app with flyctl certs add and print the CNAME target for the owner, and make the signing warning of docs/site/docs/concepts/one-account.md say the name redirects to paxportwallet.com."
verify_cmd = "timeout 20m cargo test --locked --manifest-path agent/Cargo.toml -p layerx-crypto account_derivation"
symbols    = ["account_derivation"]
touches    = ["agent/crates/layerx-crypto/src/account_derivation.rs", "agent/sdk/python/layerx_sdk/account_derivation.py", "agent/sdk/typescript/src/account-derivation.ts", "platform/sdk/conformance/fixtures/account-derivation-v1.json", "platform/hosted/human/material.py", "platform/hosted/human/test_material.py", "docs/site/docs/concepts/one-account.md", "interop/deploy/search-front/nginx.conf"]
tests      = ["agent/crates/layerx-crypto/src/account_derivation.rs"]
reqs       = ["3.4"]
